    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This report tabulates analyses for 291 samples of rock\r\ncollected by the United States Geological Survey (USGS), 662\r\nsamples of stream sediment collected during the United States\r\nDepartment of Energy-sponsored National Uranium Resource\r\nEvaluation (NURE) program and re-analyzed for this report, and\r\n449 samples of stream sediment collected by the USGS. All\r\nsamples are from the Coconino National Forest and vicinity,\r\nCoconino, Gila, and Yavapai Counties, Arizona. The analyses of\r\nthese samples can be used to evaluate the mineral resource\r\npotential of the forest and to identify areas that may contain\r\npotential environmental problems.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
